    <briefdescription>
<para>Controls Nagle&apos;s algorithm and TCP_CORK on a single socket. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Three modes are supported:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>NODELAY : TCP_NODELAY=1, TCP_CORK=0. Every write is sent immediately. Best for request-response workloads where latency matters.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>CORK : TCP_CORK=1, TCP_NODELAY=0. Segments are held until the MTU is filled or cork is released. Best for bulk streaming.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>DEFAULT : Neither flag is set. The kernel&apos;s Nagle algorithm applies (200 ms coalescing window).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Usage with batch writes: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_nagle_controller_1a9380216703dce854f70d940442a79d1f" kindref="member">NagleController</ref><sp/>nagle(<ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_nagle_controller_1a7f9d19868c7ab47af6b22a47a92b6544" kindref="member">fd</ref>);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">nagle.cork();<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>hold<sp/>data</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>...<sp/>schedule<sp/>multiple<sp/>writes<sp/>...</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">nagle.uncork();<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>flush<sp/>all<sp/>at<sp/>once</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
